<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>true</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Every Akka package moves together. The satellites (Hosting, the TestKits) ship on
    their own cadence and have historically trailed core; letting a bump move core ahead
    of them produces binding failures that surface at runtime rather than at build time.
    One property makes the coupling explicit and the upgrade deliberate.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AkkaVersion>1.5.71</AkkaVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Akka.NET">
    <PackageVersion Include="Akka" Version="$(AkkaVersion)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Akka.Hosting" Version="$(AkkaVersion)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Akka.TestKit.Xunit" Version="$(AkkaVersion)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Akka.Hosting.TestKit" Version="$(AkkaVersion)" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Persistence">
    <PackageVersion Include="MongoDB.Driver" Version="3.11.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    xUnit v3 on Microsoft Testing Platform.

    MTP replaces VSTest: a test project is a self-hosting executable rather than a library
    a runner loads, so Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk and xunit.runner.visualstudio are gone -
    xunit.v3 ships the MTP entry point itself. Coverage comes from the MTP extension
    instead of coverlet's VSTest collector.

    The Akka TestKit for v3 is Akka.TestKit.Xunit - the UNSUFFIXED name - while
    Akka.TestKit.Xunit2 is the v2 one. There is no Xunit3-suffixed package, which is what
    makes a name search wrongly conclude v3 is unsupported.

    xunit.v3 is pinned to Akka's line (3.2.x) rather than latest so the extensibility
    contract matches; FsCheck.Xunit.v3 is held at 3.3.4 for the same reason.

    No coverage extension yet: Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.CodeCoverage 18.9.0 pulls
    Microsoft.Testing.Platform 2.3.0, which xunit.v3 3.2.2 does not target - the run dies
    with a TypeLoadException on IDataConsumer. Add coverage back when the two lines meet.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Testing">
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.v3" Version="3.2.2" />
    <PackageVersion Include="FsCheck.Xunit.v3" Version="3.3.4" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Testcontainers.MongoDb" Version="4.15.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing" Version="10.0.2" />
    <PackageVersion Include="BenchmarkDotNet" Version="0.15.8" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Transitive pin. Akka.Hosting pulls OpenTelemetry.Api 1.10.0, which carries two known
    advisories (GHSA-8785-wc3w-h8q6, GHSA-g94r-2vxg-569j). Central transitive pinning
    lifts it to a patched version without waiting on an Akka release. Remove this once
    Akka.Hosting depends on a clean version on its own.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Transitive pins">
    <PackageVersion Include="OpenTelemetry.Api" Version="1.18.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
